### answer turn 1 (first 500 chars): Fervo Energy's most recent announcements (as of early October 2026):  1. Commercial operation at Cape Station — October 1, 2026 (headline news) Fervo announced that its first power plant at Cape Station in Beaver County, Utah, reached commercial operation, making it the first greenfield enhanced geothermal systems (EGS) development in the world to achieve contractual commercial operations. Key details:  The first GeoBlock synchronized to the grid on September 24 and declared commercial operation
### answer turn 2 (first 500 chars): Cape Station reached commercial operation ahead of schedule (Sept 30 / announced Oct 1–2, 2026): The first 33 MW GeoBlock synchronized to the grid and was declared commercially operational one day before its contractual COD, making it the world's first greenfield enhanced geothermal (EGS) plant to hit contractual commercial operations — built in just 23 months. Remaining Phase I GeoBlocks (~100 MW total) are targeted by January 1, 2027, with a 400 MW Phase II expected in 2028. — Sources: Fervo E
